l,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":true,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117122","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117122","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117122.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117122.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"* Part of #111218 \r\n\r\nThis PR aims to split the `Variant::Type` enum and associated methods into a new `variant_type.h` header. Doing so will enable us to reduce the amount of `variant.h` includers (which comes with its own baggage of includes), which will help both compile and recompile times. \r\n\r\nThe first (and, for now, only) commit splits `Variant::Type` and methods into `variant_type.h`, which is then included by `variant.h`.\r\n\r\nIf we decide that this is indeed the direction we want to go, a second commit will be added that adds `#include \"variant_type.h\"` explicitly everywhere it is used. This will then be supplemented by a third commit (or maybe a follow-up PR), which aims to remove all unnecessary `variant.h` includes. \r\n\r\n*I do not have either follow-up commits ready yet. The second should be easy, but the third won't be, so I don't want to pre-emptively bother if we decide this isn't the way we want things to go. As such, I cannot evaluate yet how much of a benefit this change will have, although it is expected to be significant.*\r\n\r\nDraft for now as we discuss things","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117122/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117122/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}